                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f654328-0b6d-3bc0-8987-0c127b3f04bf",
                        "entry_id": "dc5fdd7e-d91e-345b-b75e-28415a9a1d8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "tolerance"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f26c6d6-80c5-4ff7-a39b-b9b5d4a14278",
                                "sense_id": "6f654328-0b6d-3bc0-8987-0c127b3f04bf",
                                "text": "Спра́ва блесте́ла золоты́ми цепя́ми рези́новая же́нщина — из тех, что де́лают в Биг Би́зе. Же́нщин кага́н не люби́л, о чём зна́ли все. Э́то был про́сто си́мвол ста́туса, толера́нтности и гото́вности к межкульту́рному диало́гу.",
                                "translation": "On the Kagan’s right, glittering with gold chains, was a rubber woman, the kind they make in Big Byz. The Kagan didn’t like women, everyone knew that. It was merely a status symbol, a declaration of tolerance and willingness for intercultural dialogue.",
                                "english": "On the Kagan’s right, glittering with gold chains, was a rubber woman, the kind they make in Big Byz. The Kagan didn’t like women, everyone knew that. It was merely a status symbol, a declaration of tolerance and willingness for intercultural dialogue."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
